hostname r4
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.4/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to r3:eth2
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.34.2/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON R4
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP
!   configure
!   router bgp 65004
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.4
!      neighbor 10.1.34.1 remote-as 65003
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.34.1 activate
!         network 10.0.0.4/32
!      !
!
! TASK 2 — Verify filtering effects end-to-end
!   Baseline (no filters): r4 should see all prefixes from r1, r2, r3, r4.
!   show bgp ipv4 unicast
!
!   Expected (no filters):
!     10.0.0.1/32  — via AS-path: 65003 65002 65001
!     10.0.0.2/32  — via AS-path: 65003 65002
!     10.0.0.3/32  — via AS-path: 65003
!     10.0.0.4/32  — local
!     172.16.1.0/24 — via AS-path: 65003 65002 65001
!     172.16.2.0/24 — via AS-path: 65003 65002 65001
!
!   After r2 blocks 172.16.2.0/24 inbound:
!     172.16.2.0/24 should be ABSENT on r4 (blocked at r2, never forwarded)
!
!   After r3 applies AS-path filter (only accept origin AS65001):
!     10.0.0.2/32 and 10.0.0.3/32 may be absent on r4
!     (r3 blocks routes where AS65001 is NOT the origin)
!
! TASK 3 — Apply an inbound prefix-list on r4
!   Only accept prefixes in the 10.0.0.0/8 space:
!
!   ip prefix-list ONLY-RFC1918-10 seq 5 permit 10.0.0.0/8 le 32
!   ip prefix-list ONLY-RFC1918-10 seq 10 deny 0.0.0.0/0 le 32
!
!   router bgp 65004
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.34.1 prefix-list ONLY-RFC1918-10 in
!      !
!
!   After: 172.16.x.x prefixes will be absent from r4's table
!   even if r3 forwarded them.
! ============================================================
end
